sample_errors:
Terminal errors: 400 (bad_request.invalid_cursor) - client must drop cursor and restart; 403 (forbidden) - credentials/ACL issue; 422 (bad_request.unprocessable) - input semantic failure (no retry). Transient errors: 429 (rate_limit.exceeded) - retry with backoff and preserve cursor; 503 (service_unavailable.transient) - retry with exponential backoff; 500 (server_error) - treated as transient for up to 3 attempts. Error payload shape: {
  "code": "namespace.code",
  "message": "human readable",
  "retry_after_seconds": number | null,
  "cursor_safe_to_reuse": boolean
}. Map legacy numeric/http-only error shapes to this envelope at the adapter boundary.
